    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40819" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕflŭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		refluo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>flowing back</i>, <i>refluent</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					7, 267</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 97, 100, § 220</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amnes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					5, 624</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aestus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					15, 226</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gurges,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 5, 1, 91</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litus,</span>”
				<i>from which the sea recedes</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 4, p. 156</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">assueti refluas dominorum lambere micas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sedul. Carm. Pasch. 3, 246</span></i>
			.</div>
